/*
 * Canonical opcode effects sidecar for rxops.h.
 *
 * Every dense opcode slot has exactly one entry. RXE records conservative
 * possible explicit reads/writes, proven kills, branch-target operands,
 * implicit register effects, and semantic side effects. Keep entries in
 * opcode order; test_rxop_metadata validates alignment and completeness.
 * RXOP_EFFECT_KNOWN additionally certifies complete callback-route inventory;
 * it never removes resource hooks described by the writer/copy/ABI contracts.
 * Ordinary RXOP_EFFECT rows retain unknown additional callback routes.
 * RXEW/RXEVW/RXECW/RXEVCW additionally own per-operand writer signatures:
 * s = successful shared setter (reference/native prewrite release), f =
 * reviewed field/copy without that release, 0 = no explicit write, and ? =
 * unknown/special. Omitted signatures stay unknown for written operands.
 * Hidden/indexed results and alias-conditional set_value_string helpers are
 * not unconditional explicit setters. Whole-value/ABI effects remain separate.
 */
